AnonSync bounded causal replica product spine

Commands:
  anonsync_replica certificate-spki --certificate ABSOLUTE_PEM
  anonsync_replica status --replica-db ABSOLUTE_DB --folder ID --local-device ID --local-epoch N [--payload-root ABSOLUTE_DIR] [--effect-db ABSOLUTE_DB --files-root ABSOLUTE_DIR] [--membership-db ABSOLUTE_DB --anchor-db ABSOLUTE_DB]
  anonsync_replica enqueue-file --replica-db ABSOLUTE_DB --payload-root ABSOLUTE_DIR --folder ID --local-device ID --local-epoch N --destination-device ID [--destination-device ID...] --canonical-path PATH --source-file ABSOLUTE_FILE
  anonsync_replica membership-publish --membership-db ABSOLUTE_DB --anchor-db ABSOLUTE_DB --folder ID --local-device ID --local-epoch N --policy-epoch N [--peer DEVICE:EPOCH:SPKI_SHA256 ...]
  anonsync_replica send-one --replica-db ABSOLUTE_DB --payload-root ABSOLUTE_DIR --folder ID --local-device ID --local-epoch N --remote-device ID --remote-epoch N --remote-spki SHA256 --address NUMERIC_IP --port N --certificate ABSOLUTE_PEM --private-key ABSOLUTE_PEM --ca-file ABSOLUTE_PEM [--worker ID] [--lease-seconds N] [--timeout-seconds N] [--operator-clock-authority-id ID --operator-clock-uncertainty-ns N]
  anonsync_replica serve-one --replica-db ABSOLUTE_DB --effect-db ABSOLUTE_DB --membership-db ABSOLUTE_DB --anchor-db ABSOLUTE_DB --files-root ABSOLUTE_DIR --folder ID --local-device ID --local-epoch N --bind-address NUMERIC_IP --port N --certificate ABSOLUTE_PEM --private-key ABSOLUTE_PEM --ca-file ABSOLUTE_PEM [--timeout-seconds N]

All database, directory, and credential paths must be absolute. status emits a bounded attested condition report using the same durable owners as send and serve. send-one and serve-one own exactly one bounded TLS conversation; they are intentionally not a background daemon. send-one defaults to the fail-closed kernel clock source. The paired operator-clock options are an explicit deployment assertion for environments where clock synchronization evidence is externally owned. JSON is written to stdout and diagnostics to stderr.
